IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sge-p10a-361`

-- Tests of s 361 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration: effect of registration). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the
-- assertion, before the run. The notice specifies 1 March 2027 as the date of registration.

§ `Section 361(1)(a): a company as defined in section 4(1)`

-- Arguments: a notice has been issued; the date of registration it specifies; the date asked about.
-- "Starting on the date of registration": on that date and after it, deemed a company.
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the foreign corporate entity is a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the foreign corporate entity is a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day before, it is not: a body incorporated outside Singapore is not "a company incorporated under this Act".
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the foreign corporate entity is a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 28 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No notice issued: no date of registration, so no deeming.
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the foreign corporate entity is a company as defined in section 4(1)` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: notice issued; date of registration; date asked; the provision pertains to companies; the regulations adapt it for the entity.
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity`
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity as the regulations adapt, except or modify it`
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the text does not say whether the provision applies to the entity`
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 28 2 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision does not yet apply to the entity`
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(a) the provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 2 3 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision does not yet apply to the entity`

§ `Section 361(1)(b): the end of registration as a foreign company`

-- Arguments: notice issued; date of registration; date asked; was registered as a foreign company immediately before.
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(b) the foreign corporate entity has ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day before the date of registration it is still registered: the paragraph starts on that date.
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(b) the foreign corporate entity has ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 28 2 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not registered as a foreign company immediately before: "if" it was; otherwise the paragraph ends no such registration.
#ASSERT `s 361(1)(b) the foreign corporate entity has ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 2 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 361(2): what registration does not do`

-- Registered: each flat negative answers JUST FALSE. Not registered: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(a) the registration of the foreign corporate entity creates a new legal entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(a) the registration of the foreign corporate entity creates a new legal entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(b) the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudices or affects the thing` TRUE `s 361(2)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(b) the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudices or affects the thing` TRUE `s 361(2)(b) the continuity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity as a body corporate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(b) the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudices or affects the thing` FALSE `s 361(2)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(c) the registration of the foreign corporate entity affects the thing` TRUE `s 361(2)(c) the property of the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(c) the registration of the foreign corporate entity affects the thing` TRUE `s 361(2)(c) the rights of the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(c) the registration of the foreign corporate entity affects the thing` TRUE `s 361(2)(c) the obligations of the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(c) the registration of the foreign corporate entity affects the thing` FALSE `s 361(2)(c) the rights of the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(d) the registration of the foreign corporate entity renders defective legal proceedings by or against the foreign corporate entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 361(2)(d) the registration of the foreign corporate entity renders defective legal proceedings by or against the foreign corporate entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: registered; the proceedings could have been continued or commenced before registration.
#ASSERT `s 361(2) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Proceedings that could not have been continued or commenced before: the grant is for those that could, and the text says nothing of the rest.
#ASSERT `s 361(2) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 361(2) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
